#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:539
msgid "Frequently Asked Questions"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:543
msgid "Where is my sitemap?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:544
msgid "Your sitemap is generated dynamically at /sitemap.xml. No physical file is created, keeping your server clean."
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:547
msgid "Does a high SEO score guarantee rankings?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:548
msgid "No. The score summarizes local editorial checks. Use it to review useful titles, descriptions, structure and links, not as a ranking prediction or a reason to repeat keywords unnaturally."
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:551
msgid "Will this slow down my site?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:552
msgid "VonSEO uses native WordPress storage and bounded audit/sitemap batches. Actual performance depends on your hosting, content, theme and other plugins."
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:559
msgid "SEO & Indexing Disclaimer"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:562
msgid "VonSEO provides technical and editorial SEO tools. Installing or using this plugin does not guarantee that your website or any page will be crawled, indexed, ranked or displayed by Google or any other search engine. No indexing deadline, ranking position, traffic increase or rich result is promised."
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:563
msgid "Sitemaps, metadata, structured data, canonical hints and optional IndexNow notifications support SEO workflows; they do not force search engines to accept or index a URL. Search engines independently decide what to crawl, index and show. VonSEO scores are internal editorial checks, not Google scores or proof of indexing."
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:564
msgid "Google Search Essentials"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:570
msgid "Privacy & Data Policy"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:573
msgid "Local data and public output"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:574
msgid "VonSEO has no built-in telemetry or analytics tracking. It stores settings in WordPress options and SEO fields in post/term metadata, without custom database tables. Content analysis runs in your browser and Site Audit runs on your WordPress server. Public metadata, schema and business details are readable by visitors and crawlers; publish only information intended for the public."
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:575
msgid "Optional local diagnostics and browser preferences"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:576
msgid "If you enable 404 logging, VonSEO stores up to 50 requested URLs locally, with a hit count and last-hit time. URLs can include query strings and personal information; avoid sensitive URL parameters. This log does not store visitor IP addresses or user-agent strings. Turning logging off stops new entries but does not erase existing ones; deleting the plugin removes the local 404 log. The settings screen uses browser sessionStorage only to remember the active settings tab, not to identify visitors or send tracking data."
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:577
msgid "Optional IndexNow requests"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:578
msgid "IndexNow defaults to off unless you previously enabled it. When enabled, your server sends eligible canonical content URLs, site hostname, verification key and key-file location to Bing and Yandex. Those services also receive ordinary HTTP request information such as the server IP address. Draft text, post bodies and SEO descriptions are not sent. Turn IndexNow off in Advanced to stop future notifications; deactivation also clears queued events. A delivered request cannot be recalled."
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:579
msgid "IndexNow documentation"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:579
msgid "Microsoft privacy"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:579
msgid "Yandex privacy"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:580
msgid "Manual Competitor scans"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:581
msgid "Only an authorized editor can request a Competitor scan for enabled content. Your server fetches the URL that editor enters; the destination can see the requested URL, server IP address and normal request headers. Editor drafts are not uploaded to that destination or an AI service. Results use a WordPress transient with a 12-hour expiry. The destination website has its own privacy policy."
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:582
msgid "Manual validation and external links"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:583
msgid "Schema testing buttons open Google or Schema.org and pass a page URL, falling back to the current editor URL if a permalink is unavailable. The external service receives normal browser request information; inspect the URL before submitting confidential addresses. Documentation and donation links also lead to third-party sites with their own privacy policies. These are user-initiated links, not background telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:584
msgid "Public llms.txt"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:585
msgid "When enabled on a public site, llms.txt is a public text endpoint, not a private document or an access-control mechanism. Manually curated text and links are not checked individually for password/noindex eligibility. Do not put secrets or private links there. Disabling the endpoint or making the site non-public returns a 404, but cannot erase copies already fetched by third parties."
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:586
msgid "Retention and removal"
msgstr ""

#: admin/partials/vonseowp-admin-display.php:587
msgid "Deactivation retains saved settings and SEO fields. Deleting VonSEO runs its settings and metadata cleanup, including taxonomy SEO fields and cached Competitor scans. Site backups, hosting/server logs and data already received by external services are outside this cleanup. Adapt your public site privacy notice to the services and hosting you actually use; this plugin notice does not replace it."
msgstr ""

